# Classic Era only for now, deliberately. The 32/16 caps and the world-buff economy that make this
# addon worth having are Classic facts; a Retail .toc would ship a number that means nothing there.
# Other flavours arrive as extra .toc files over the same file list once Era is proven — the flavour
# branch is confined to BoonkeeperCompat.lua so that stays a packaging change, not a fork.
#
# Load order matters: each module reads the ones above it out of the Boonkeeper namespace at load.
# BoonkeeperCore is pure and is covered by Tests/ under plain Lua.
BoonkeeperCompat.lua
BoonkeeperCore.lua
BoonkeeperScan.lua
BoonkeeperProbe.lua
BoonkeeperDisplay.lua

# The bootstrap binds the modules together, so it loads last.
Boonkeeper.lua
